# Copy this file into EACH app repo as `.dockerignore` (next to package.json).
# It keeps junk out of the build context → smaller, faster, safer images.
# The single most important line is `.env` — never bake secrets into an image.
#
# Patterns match from the context ROOT. `*.md` matches only root-level files;
# `**/*.md` matches at any depth. (Measured 29.9: with `*.md` alone the backend
# image still carried docs/*.md, src/test and the jest config.)

node_modules
npm-debug.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git
.github
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
coverage
dist
build
.vscode
.idea
**/*.md

# Tests and test/lint tooling — never needed at runtime.
**/*.test.js
**/*.int.test.js
**/test
jest.config.*
jest.*.js
jest.*.cjs
.babelrc
.eslintrc*
.prettierrc*
nodemon.json
e2e
playwright-report
test-results
